      "writtenOn": "2019-10-17T21:55:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like we define simple macros (e.g. test_mockable) differently depending on TEST_BUILD or TEST_FUZZ.\n\nOne advantage of fuzz_noreturn is that the condition can be changed at once. For example,\n\n  #ifdef TEST_FUZZ\n  #define fuzz_noreturn __attribute__((noreturn))\n  #endif\n\ncan be changed to\n\n  #if defined(TEST_FUZZ) || defined(TEST_BUILD)\n  #define fuzz_noreturn __attribute__((noreturn))\n  #endif\n\nwhile with ATTRIBUTE_IF, conditions are distributed.\n\nSo, being consistent with other similar macros, checkpatch spitting warning, and the advantage mentioned above, I would vote for fuzz_noreturn.",
